## Milestones

| M-ID | Title | Inputs | Output | Status | Est. pages |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| M1 | <title> (under T1.1) | <inputs> | `<output/path>` | pending | <N> |
| M2 | <title> (under T1.1) | <inputs> | `<output/path>` | pending | <N> |
| M3 | <title> (under T2.1) | <inputs> | `<output/path>` | pending | <N> |

<!--
Milestones answer "when." One Milestone = one execution pass = one named output
file (R2). The shape that triggers a split is a title joined by "and" or a row
whose body would carry bullet sub-items. Split before writing the row.

Milestones use a flat global counter — M1, M2, M3 — so each Milestone ID stays
unique across the whole project. The "(under T1.1)" tag in the Title column
names the parent Target. Sub-letter expansion (M1a, M1b) lands when atomic
units cluster under one row; each sub-letter is its own ledger row per R8.

Status values: pending | in_progress | done | ~~sunset~~.
Sunset Milestones stay in the ledger forever per R9 (strikethrough, never delete).

Inputs column lists the files the execution pass reads (R3). Anything not listed
is not in scope for the pass. The pass re-reads the listed Inputs at the start of
every execution — state does not carry across passes.

Est. pages is a small-integer estimate that helps the dispatch protocol decide
whether to delegate to a subagent (R10).
-->

